      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Event-horizon-scale images converted a long-standing theoretical frontier into a direct astronomical measurement.",
        "attribution": "Falcke advanced the black-hole-shadow target, Doeleman led the interferometric realization, and Narayan represents essential theoretical interpretation.",
        "maturity": "The initial black-hole image has been followed by additional imaging and polarization results, with broad scrutiny of calibration and reconstruction.",
        "uncertainties": [
